/*
:name: mclk_derived
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: mclk_derived.derived
:pyrope_top: derived
*/

// Multi-clock registers with a GATED clock. `qa` is clocked by `clock`; `qb` is
// clocked by `gclk`, a `wire` holding the ICG `Clock(clock_pin=clk_b,
// enable=gate)` (ruling 56: the one derived Clock; the golden spells the same
// ICG as a latch + AND). Two bugs used to break this:
//   1. upass/ssa did not SSA-rename the `attr_set ... clock_pin <wire>` value
//      operand, so the clock_pin resolved to the declaration-time `gclk = 0ub?`
//      poison instead of the live `gclk___ssa_1` driver — the flop bound to an
//      unknown const (cgen emitted `posedge invalid_*`).
//   2. inou/cgen emitted the clock with `pin_wire_name` (dropping the `_u`
//      unsigned suffix / not handling an inlined single-fanout clock node), so
//      the `always @(posedge ...)` referenced an undeclared net.
// Both are fixed; prp->verilog is LEC-equivalent to the golden below.
mod derived(clock:Clock, clk_b:Clock, gate:Bool, da:U8, db:U8) -> (qa:U8@[1], qb:U8@[1]) {
  reg qa:U8:[clock_pin=clock] = 0
  qa = da
  wire gclk:Clock = nil
  gclk = Clock(clock_pin=clk_b, enable=gate)
  // ASYNC reset, matching the golden. A SYNC reset on a GATED clock is swallowed
  // whenever the gate is low through reset (gclk never rises), so the two sides
  // could only agree by accident -- and lgcheck, which is edge-blind here, calls
  // it a difference. Async is the correct spelling for a gated flop.
  reg qb:U8:[clock_pin=gclk, async=true] = 0
  qb = db
}
